Job Title: Coordinator II – Customer Advocacy
Location: Rhode Island (Statewide Travel Required)
Duration: 12 Months
Interview: Virtual / In-Person
Work Arrangement: Field-Based

Job Description
We are seeking a customer-focused Coordinator II to support RI Energy's income-eligible and vulnerable customers. The candidate will help customers access energy assistance programs, manage utility bills, arrange payments, and connect with community support services.
The role involves working with customers, community action agencies, advocacy groups, and internal teams to improve awareness and participation in energy assistance programs.
Key Responsibilities
•	Assist customers with billing, payments, payment arrangements, LIHEAP, outage preparedness, and energy efficiency programs.
•	Build relationships with community agencies, advocacy groups, and internal stakeholders.
•	Manage and prioritize customer referrals and provide tailored solutions for special cases.
•	Conduct community outreach and represent RI Energy at customer assistance events.
•	Gather customer feedback and recommend improvements to assistance programs.
•	Prepare training materials, brochures, and supporting documentation.
•	Ensure compliance with company policies, procedures, and applicable regulations.
Required Qualifications
•	Bilingual communication skills required; Spanish preferred.
•	Bachelor's degree preferred, with 3+ years of relevant customer advocacy or customer service experience.
•	Experience supporting low-income customers or working with social service programs is preferred.
•	Strong communication, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and relationship-building skills.
•	Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and Access.
•	Ability to learn customer information systems, energy assistance programs, and company procedures.
Travel Requirements
•	Statewide travel throughout Rhode Island is required.
•	Candidates must have their own vehicle.
•	Travel to community action agencies is expected approximately three times per week.
•	Qualifying mileage beyond the normal round-trip commute to Johnston, RI, is reimbursed according to company policy.
Ideal Candidate: A compassionate and organized professional with strong customer service skills and experience in customer advocacy, community outreach, social services, or utility assistance programs.


